{
  "$comment": "THE TREE (lib/sessions/send.ts startRoot/startChild/reviveRoot/continueSession, lifecycle.ts, trpc sessions.claim/report). ONE tree per thread: a root (depth 0, rootId = its id) and children (parentId, rootId inherited, depth + 1). Every new session is `queued` on a device with its first message PENDING: a caller session's message is agent-authored (`authorSessionId` = the caller), a person's is user-authored; a blank text posts nothing. A child posts a `session` card on its parent (informational). A root started from inside a session is WATCHED by it (wakeOn) and posts `thread_started` on it; its device defaults to the caller root's when that tree has an acting agent, else none = refused (`invalid`). CAPS (rules.caps): a child deeper than treeMaxDepth = `invalid`, a tree already at treeMaxSessions LIVE sessions = `limit`; an ended branch frees its slot. CLAIM: only the named device (`conflict`), never an ended row; queued → running, startedAt stamped once, an `unclaimed` flag clears; the FIRST claim delivers the first input as the brief's Request (consumed, the `brief` effect names it, sealed or not: #FEED-178) and says `session_claimed` to the listeners (non-waking, no self fallback). A message to an ENDED thread root REVIVES the same row (idle, nothing flagged, message pending); to an ENDED child it CONTINUES as a new sibling (`freshId`; same parent and depth; the caps apply; a `session` card on the parent); with no text it is refused. END: a root's End ends its whole live tree, a child's its subtree, deepest first then oldest first; each row flips ended (busy/needsInput/blocked cleared), its open ask mirrors close, it says `session_ended` on itself and REPORTS into its parent and watchers (bus.json); then each is killed. An agent's conversation never ends (its children do). A device report `status: ended` (the process is gone) ends a child and a root that never finished a turn (a refused launch); a root that finished one and an agent's conversation go idle instead.",
